course: dictionary
lesson: 9495
title: Words from the past
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words are about things that lived millions of years ago. You can work out what they mean by reading the clues around them. «Stegosaurus had two rows of tall thin plates for show and four tail spikes that were a real weapon.» Plates are flat bony pieces, and a weapon is something used to fight.
explain: The name itself is a clue. Stegosaurus means «roof lizard». People gave it that name because they thought its plates lay flat like roof tiles. Use the parts of a word to help you, just as you use the words around it.
explain: Check your meaning by putting it into the sentence. «Plant-eaters were not helpless: Stegosaurus had tail spikes.» If helpless means unable to protect yourself, then the spikes make sense as a way to fight back. If your meaning does not fit, try another one.
fact: «Stegosaurus» means «roof lizard».
fact: A stegosaurus was a large plant-eating dinosaur with two rows of big bony plates along its back and sharp spikes on its tail.
fact: Its spiked tail is called a thagomizer, and it used the spikes to defend itself.
fact: Stegosaurus lived long before «T. rex», so the two never met.
exercise: Why did people call it «roof lizard»? | They thought it was very small | *They thought its back plates looked like flat roof tiles | They thought it lived on roofs | They thought it had a roof-shaped head
exercise: «Stegosaurus had four tail spikes that were a real weapon.» What does weapon mean? | *Something used to fight or defend | A kind of plant food | A bony plate on its back | A tiny brain
exercise: «Plant-eaters were not helpless.» What does helpless mean here? | *Unable to protect themselves | Hungry all the time | Very tall | Happy and calm
test: «Stegosaurus had a tiny brain for its big body.» What does tiny mean? | Very big | Very clever | Very old | *Very small
test: What is a thagomizer used for? | To keep warm | To catch fish | *To defend itself | To dig holes
exam: «Stegosaurus lived about 150 million years ago, so more time separates Stegosaurus from T. rex than separates T. rex from us.» Which statement is true? | Stegosaurus lived after people | T. rex lived before Stegosaurus | Stegosaurus and T. rex met each other | *Stegosaurus lived long before T. rex
